# Settings

Organisation configuration lives under `/settings`, not as its own item in the main workforce navigation. Email follow-ups are the exception: they live under Work at `/workflows`.

The section list is `lib/settings-sections.ts`. The settings layout renders that list. Each section is a page at `app/(app)/settings/<section>/page.tsx` and uses `SettingsFrame`.

Groups are Account and Organisation. Account is personal and available to every signed-in person. Organisation is administrator configuration (`audience: "admin"`).

When a feature needs configuration — templates, schedules, toggles, destinations, or anything an administrator sets once for the organisation — do both of these in the same change:

1. Add a section to `settingsSections` with a group, audience, label, href, and one-line description.
2. Add the page under `app/(app)/settings/` and link any in-product control to that section.

Do not add a new top-level nav item for that configuration. Do not leave a feature's settings only on the feature page.
